    "q-95725": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95725",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-9,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$",
      "worked_solution": "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot \\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-65 & 78 \\\\ 78 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95725-a",
